 10%: cents = 10000, discount = 10000 * 10 / 100 = 1000.0, int(1000.0 + 0.5) = 1000, (10000-1000)/100 = 90.0 ✓\\n\\nAll good. The fix is to change `int(cents * pct / 100)` to `int(cents * pct / 100 + 0.5)`.\\n\\nLet me also check: is there ANY rounding happening on `round(price * 100)` that could be an issue too? Let me check each test case:\\n\\n- 100.0 * 100 = 10000.0 → round(10000.0) = 10000 ✓ (as int, then int)\\n- 19.99 * 100 = 1999.0 → round(1999.0) = 1999 ✓ (1999.0 is exact)\\n- 12.50 * 100 = 1250.0 → round(1250.0) = 1250 ✓ (1250.0 is exact)\\n- 9.80 * 100 = 980.0 → round(980.0) = 980 ✓\\n- 10.20 * 100 = 1020.0 → round(1020.0) = 1020 ✓\\n\\nAll exact. Good. The issue is purely the truncation of the discount.\\n\\nNow let me also check if there are any SPEC examples that the test doesn't cover, to see if they also pass:\\n\\n- 9.80 at 2.5%: price*100 = 980.0, round = 980, discount = 980*2.5/100 = 24.5, int(24.5 + 0.5) = 25, result = 9.55 ✓\\n- 10.20 at 2.5%: 1020, discount = 25.5, int(25.5+0.5)=26, result = 9.94 ✓\\n\\nGood.\\n\\nLet me make the fix. I'll also update the docstring since it currently says \\\"truncated, not rounded\\\" which contradicts the SPEC.\"}],\"summary\":[],\"format\":\"unknown\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2f739e843bca43ab93807d05|fc_tmp_tpbm46dshsq","name":"edit","arguments":{"i":"Fix discount rounding to HALF UP per SPEC","new_string":"\"\"\"The price after a `pct` percent discount.\"\"\"\n    cents = int(round(price * 100))\n    discount = int(cents * pct / 100 + 0.5)   # rounded HALF UP\n    return (cents - discount) / 100.0","old_string":"\"\"\"The price after a `pct` percent discount.\"\"\"\n    cents = int(round(price * 100))\n    discount = int(cents * pct / 100)          # truncated, not rounded\n    return (cents - discount) / 100.0","path":"money/round.py","replace_all":false},"intent":"Fix discount rounding to HALF UP per SPEC"}],"api":"openrouter","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"